{
  "bridge_text": "寒风吹动了莉娜的红外套，她在那棵大树的阴影下停住了脚步，树干里传出的低鸣声仿佛在邀请她一探究竟。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "在那棵大树的阴影下，莉娜并没有退缩，而是推开了那扇虚掩的树皮门。她迈出的每一步都显得格外小心，仿佛生怕惊扰了这寒夜里的秘密。树干里隐约透出的光，引领着她走向那道通往未知深处的入口。"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "走进树干，她发现了一道盘旋向下的楼梯，台阶上坐着一只穿着补丁绿背心的老灰狐狸。那狐狸名叫莫斯克，他用干树叶摩擦般的嗓音告诉莉娜，这棵树不是用来参观的，她应该回家忘掉那阵低鸣。可莉娜摇了摇头，她说自己无法忘记那些还没听到的故事。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of Mosk's grumpiness remains tucked away in the shadows of the tree, but Lina is determined to see what lies beneath. She stands her ground on the top step, waiting to see if the fox will truly let her pass.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes meeting the fox's weary gaze. She knew the humming was no accident, and she was not about to turn back now. Mosk let out a long, ragged sigh that ruffled the fur on his chest, but he did not move to push her away."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Mosk, the fox with the green vest, watched Lina closely as he waited for her to turn back toward the woods. With the path ahead still waiting, Lina held her ground.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a thin, gray paw at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket instead. She pulled out the very last apple of the autumn season and set it gently on the step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she said softly. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time, his eyes softening. He stood up, adjusted his patched vest, and finally stepped onto the first stair without saying a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Down in the depths of the tree, the humming turned into a quiet, pulsing song. A firefly the size of a robin lay curled on a bed of soft moss, her golden glow flickering and dim. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had once been his closest friend, but he had failed to bring her medicine during a harsh winter long ago. He had guarded this tree ever since, too ashamed to face her until now."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
