{
  "bridge_text": "With the soft moss cradling her like a velvet blanket, the firefly lay still as the shadows deepened. Mosk moved closer, his heart heavy with the weight of that long-ago winter.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming was a quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin rested upon a thick, velvet-green bed of moss, her light flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. She had been his friend once, but in a winter long past, he had arrived too late with her medicine. Ever since, he had guarded this hollow tree, shielding her light while hiding his own deep shame."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the gentle moss, asking the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen replied softly, for that was all true medicine ever was. Mosk quickly fetched the milk in a silver thimble, resting his paw beside hers. As the queen’s glow steadied, the humming inside the tree blossomed into a new, beautiful tune, and for the first time in years, Mosk hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
