{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk settled on that top step, his patched vest catching the dim light, Lina stood firm before him. She listened to the dry rustle of his voice as he warned her away from the tree's secrets.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, Lina discovered a narrow curl of stairs winding deep into the trunk. Perched upon the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a vest of faded green with patches at the elbows. This was Mosk. In a voice as thin and crisp as dry autumn leaves, he told Lina that no one was permitted to visit the heart of the tree, urging her to turn back and forget the strange humming she had heard. Lina looked at him, her heart steady, and told him she could not possibly forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

